  "design": "jn2_Froude_equivalent_complete_six_dof",
  "design_notes": "Target-scale CFD counterpart to the 0.7-scale jn2 PMM sweep. All six FLU DOFs use the seven measured-frequency equivalents. Surge and roll are newly excited; sway, heave, pitch and yaw repeat the PMM-covered DOFs. Starting from the converged steady-tow field, each case discards max(one oscillation period, one target-length convective time) and fits the following complete period. This is the minimum complete-cycle design: the discarded interval exposes the near-body flow to every forcing phase once, and the retained interval supplies every phase once for half-cycle odd projection. Repeated PMM records had effectively identical prescribed motion, so CFD uses one deterministic case per DOF/frequency rather than three duplicate solves.",
